-- title:
--   Deligne–Rapoport model at p ∥ M with pinned Atkin–Lehner map
-- statement:
--   Let $p$ be a prime and $M\ge 1$, let $H$ be a subgroup of $(\mathbb Z/M)^\times$, and assume $p\mid M$, $p^2\nmid M$, and that $H$ contains every unit $u$ of $(\mathbb Z/M)^\times$ whose image under the reduction $(\mathbb Z/M)^\times\to(\mathbb Z/(M/p))^\times$ is $1$; assume further that the Laurent series `jqModC ℚ` (namely $q^{-1}$ times the rational power series `jNum`) lies in `qExpFunctionFieldC ℚ ⊤`, the subfield of $\mathbb Q((q))$ generated over $\mathbb Q$ by the ratios of $q$-expansions of integral modular forms of level $SL(2,\mathbb Z)$. Then there exist: a term $\mathfrak X$ of the property bundle `XHDRModelAtP p M H hpM hj` for the two-chart model $X$ of level `ΓM M H` over `R p` (recording properness, flatness, integrality and local finite presentation of its structure morphism, normality of its affine sections, the corresponding properness and relative smoothness at the auxiliary level `ΓN`, a curve model `Meta` over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ with function field `xHFunctionFieldBar M H` together with an isomorphism `eeta` onto the base change of $X$ to $\overline{\mathbb Q}$, its Galois equivariance and chart pinning, generic smoothness and geometric integrality, and an endomorphism datum `w` of $X$, among further data); an $\overline{\mathbb Q}$-algebra automorphism $\theta$ of `xHFunctionFieldBar M H`, the subfield of $\overline{\mathbb Q}((q))$ generated over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ by the coefficientwise image of `xHFunctionField M H`; and an `R p`-algebra automorphism $\vartheta$ of `chartAlgFin p (ΓM M H) hj`, the algebra of elements of `qExpFunctionFieldC ℚ (ΓM M H)` integral over the `R p`-subalgebra generated by $j$; such that four conditions hold. First, whenever $f$ in `xHFunctionFieldBar M H` and $u$ in `xHFunctionFieldBar (M / p) (infSubgroup p M H hpM)` — the latter for the image of $H$ in $(\mathbb Z/(M/p))^\times$ — have the same underlying Laurent series, the Laurent series of $\theta f$ is `qExpand` of it at $p$, i.e. the substitution $q\mapsto q^{p}$ on exponents. Second, for any two $\overline{\mathbb Q}$-points $y,y'$ of `𝔛.Meta.C` over the base, if $y'$ followed by `eeta`, the first pullback projection and `𝔛.w.hom` agrees with $y$ followed by `eeta` and the first pullback projection, then the place `𝔛.Meta.pointEquivPlace y'` is the translate of `𝔛.Meta.pointEquivPlace y` under the semilinear automorphism $(\theta,1)$ attached to $\theta$. Third, `ιFin p (ΓM M H) hj` followed by `𝔛.w.hom` equals `Spec.map` of $\vartheta$ followed by `ιFin p (ΓM M H) hj`, and the preimage under `𝔛.w.hom` of the open range of `ιFin p (ΓM M H) hj` is that open range. Fourth, for $b$ in the chart algebra and $f$ in `xHFunctionFieldBar M H`, if the series of $f$ is the coefficientwise image of the series of $b$, then the series of $\theta f$ is the coefficientwise image of the series of $\vartheta b$.
--
--   This is the existence statement for the Deligne–Rapoport model of $X_H(M)$ over `R p` at a prime exactly dividing the level, equipped with its Atkin–Lehner automorphism, pinned simultaneously on the geometric function field (where it acts by $q\mapsto q^{p}$ on forms of level $M/p$) and on the $j$-finite integral chart, where it is the spectrum of an algebra automorphism. It feeds the level-lowering analysis at $p\parallel M$, in particular the statements on inertia acting on the Tate module of the Jacobian $J_H$ and on the mod-$\ell$ diamond and Frobenius places.
